# WHICH CHAIN THIS ESTATE IS ON. EMBER TESTNET, `hearth-testnet`, CHAIN ID 7412.
#
# The sibling of `chain.mainnet.env`, which carries the whole argument for why
# these settings are in a file at all. Read that one first; this file states only
# what differs.
#
# Loaded when `CF_EMBER_NETWORK=testnet`, which `compose/testnet.env` sets. That
# same file sets `EMBER_RPC_URL` to port 8745 — the testnet estate's OWN seed,
# brought up by `docker-compose.hearth-seed-testnet.yml` — and
# `COMPOSE_PROFILES=ember-testnet`, which is what admits the `faucet`.

# `indexer/src/evm.ts:471-480` will refuse to write a block unless the node
# answers `eth_chainId` with 7412 (`contracts/packages/chain/src/index.ts:199`).
INDEXER_CHAINS=ember:testnet,ltc:testnet

# The name is the primary key of `provider_health`; see the mainnet file.
INDEXER_RPC_EMBER_TESTNET=hearth-testnet-seed=${EMBER_RPC_URL:-http://host.docker.internal:8745}

# From genesis — a chain younger than 120 blocks cannot answer `custodyTotal` from
# a `tip − 120` cold start. See the mainnet file.
INDEXER_START_HEIGHT_EMBER_TESTNET=0

# ── LITECOIN, AS REGTEST ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The mainnet file says there is no Litecoin testnet node, and that was true. It
# is no longer the whole picture: what testnet needs is not a copy of Litecoin
# but a UTXO chain whose outputs an operator can control, because that is the
# only way to prove the derivation in micro-org#252 rather than assert it. A
# derived custody balance is credits with no matching spend, and nothing proves
# that arithmetic except funding an address, spending part of it, and reading the
# number back.
#
# So this is `litecoind -regtest`, not Litecoin. `indexer/src/bitcoin.ts:471`
# accepts `regtest` as a `getblockchaininfo.chain` value for a `testnet` scope,
# and that line was written for exactly this.
#
# WALKED FROM GENESIS, and that is the half of the proof this file carries. On a
# genesis-walked record the coverage floor is 0, so an address with no history
# claim is `claim = 0 >= lo = 0` and the derivation ANSWERS. On a cold-started
# record — which `ltc:mainnet` is, floor 3,155,209 — the same unclaimed address
# refuses with `history_unknown`. Two estates, two floors, opposite outcomes from
# one rule: that is what makes the rule testable.
INDEXER_START_HEIGHT_LTC_TESTNET=0

# The URL carries basic-auth credentials, so like its mainnet sibling it lives in
# the gitignored `secrets/chainrpc.testnet.env` and is not written here. The
# regtest node binds RPC inside the `cf-testnet_default` network only; it holds a
# wallet, which the mainnet node deliberately does not, because generating blocks
# and spending outputs IS the test. There is no real money on regtest and its
# keys guard nothing.

# ── FORESIGHT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# `false` is `env.ts:374`'s own default and is written out anyway, because the
# mainnet sibling writes `true` and a reader comparing the two files should see
# the pair change together rather than one appear from nowhere.
FORESIGHT_NETWORK=testnet
FORESIGHT_MAINNET_ENABLED=false
